          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 21:54:37.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21068 tests: limit concurrent renames in sanityn/81d",
        "message": "LU-21068 tests: limit concurrent renames in sanityn/81d\n\nsanityn test_81d started one background mrename for every file,\nMDSCOUNT * COUNT = 10000 processes by default, before waiting for\nany of them.  On a 3GB aarch64 client with 16KB PAGE_SIZE thousands\nof them would be alive at once, and their page tables alone (~650MB)\nwould run the client out of memory, killing the test or an mrename.\n\nRename the files from both mounts on all MDTs together, but keep the\nmrename PIDs in a circular array of SANITYN_81d_THR (default 256)\nentries and wait for the oldest one before starting another, so that\nabout that many renames are always running.  Waiting for each PID\nalso catches a failed mrename: the existing \"wait || error\" could not,\nsince \"wait\" without arguments always returns 0.\n\nFixes: 18f5131ce588 (\"LU-17426 tests: add crossdir parallel rename test\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I536eda711020963d833428324a07eac9a93ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
